  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Anglican Alliance strategic partnership</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objectives for Year 3 (updated May 2026 based on AA proposal for Year 3 - Jan-Dec 2026)
&#xa0;1)&#xa0;&#xa0;&#xa0; Protecting the planet and communities living on the front line of climate change. Specifically to support indigenous voices in the climate debate, supporting - and possibly co-convening - an indigenous theologies conference in the Philippines in late 2026 for theologians and activists from Latin America and Asia-Pacific.&#xa0;
2)&#xa0;&#xa0; 2. Support Peace building in S Sudan: Specifically to enable Canon Grace Kaiso to continue his work of peace building in South Sudan, working with faith leaders across the region and in South Sudan to enable the church to take on more of a leadership role on speaking for peace and fair elections in the country, and for a coordinated regional church response, in connection with other partners such as AACC, FECCLAHA, WCC.
3)&#xa0;&#xa0; Gender Justice. Rolling out a short course on Men and Masculinities, for men to come together and discuss issues of masculinity within cultural contexts. The aim of the course is to transform relationships and end gender-based violence, providing a foundational household base for sustainable development. Rolling out in Brazil in August 26 with possible extension to Kenya. Ongoing collaboration around the UN CSW for March 2026 and March 2027, hoping to support participation of Archbishop Sarah Mullally.</narrative>
  </description>
